# SH-BLOCKED KNOWN GAP (Round XXXII Track D+E output-review B1, 2026-08-06):
# spawn + `&`-param on non-scalar `shared Vector` requires SH's shared
# machinery + shared-spawn dispatch. SH silently falls non-scalar `shared T`
# through to plain var-decl and DRIVER-FAILs on the runtime_diff SH lane.
#
# ⚠ THE RUST CLASS-FIX IS PROVEN: this fixture passes on BOTH Rust backends
# (C + LLVM). The integration test `shared_spawn_grow_vector` (`#[ignore]`d)
# asserts the intended `3` on the C backend. Un-ignore + move back to
# `tests/fixtures/` once the SH `op_consume` follow-up (TODO.md) lands.
#
# Cell: ArcMutex · Vector[int] · call-returned · spawn-async · pre-fix ICE 101 ·
# post-fix `3`
#
# Part of the shared-var-decl class-fix fixture net (Core #11/#12). Exercises
# the composed shape `shared T = <computed>` + `spawn f(&s)` + `t.await()` on
# a Vector inner type — pinning the async task-facade path for non-scalar
# resource inners.

async void grow(Vector[int] &xs):
    xs.push(1)
    xs.push(2)

Vector[int] seed():
    Vector[int] v = [0]
    return v

async void main():
    shared Vector[int] v = seed()
    Task[void] t = spawn grow(&v)
    t.await()
    with v:
        print(v.len())
